INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('terra-cotta-warrior', 'Terra-Cotta Warrior', 'construct', 'rifts', 0, 'Any: Principled (01-10%), Unprincipled (11-20%), Anarchist (21-50%), Miscreant (51-65%) or Aberrant (66-100%); Scrupulous and Diabolic are all but unknown', '{"IQ":"2D6+5","ME":"2D6+3","MA":"2D6+4","PS":"1D6+19","PP":"2D6+6","PE":"2D6+10","PB":"2D6+4","Spd":"1D6+4"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6+15', '2D6+15', NULL, 'The book spells this block''s title "Terra-Cotta Warrors". Race: an artificial body hosting a spirit of the dead. P.S. is Supernatural; Spd is low for a living thing even though it moves smoothly. Body M.D.C. tracks current P.P.E. (the book gives no separate figure), so spending or losing P.P.E. lowers it. Terra-cotta armor M.D.C. by location: helmet 30, main body 50, arms 14 each, legs 20 each; the armor weighs 200 lbs (90 kg) or more, gives -10% to Climb, Prowl and similar skills, and its wearer sinks in water and bogs down in deep mud. Without ambient P.P.E. body and armor are S.D.C.; Rifts Earth has enough nearly everywhere, but on other worlds or in other times they are probably S.D.C. beings with a Natural A.R. of 12. P.P.E. recovery: 1 point an hour at most, and only close to a ley (dragon) line, a nexus or another natural flow of P.P.E. Level by rank, rolled on percentile: Warrior 01-80%, 5th to 7th level Soldier; Engineering Specialist 81-90%, 5th to 7th; Scout 91-95%, 8th to 10th level Military Scout; Officer 96-99%, 10th to 12th level Military Officer, with 1D8 extra P.P.E. that also raises body M.D.C.; General 100%, 13th to 15th level Military Officer. They never gain levels. 98% are male, 2% female.', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":4,"strike":2,"parry":3,"dodge":1,"disarm":2,"pull":1,"roll":1}', 'Officers and Generals have +2 attacks. Bonuses are on top of any from attributes. +1 save vs every kind of magic, +3 save vs Horror Factor, +3 save vs possession (no bonus when a Terra-Cotta General is the one possessing).', 'Set by what the soldier had learned before dying; new skills come very slowly. Warrior (01-80%): Hand to Hand: Expert, W.P. Sword, W.P. Spear, W.P. Crossbow, Military Etiquette (+20%), Climbing (+10%), 1D8 Secondary Skills. Engineering Specialist (81-90%): the Warrior''s skills and Basic Mechanics +20%, Masonry, Whittling and Sculpting +20%, General Repair and Maintenance +15%, Carpentry +15%, Basic Math +10%, Field Armorer +10%, Military Fortification +10%, and making and repairing hand to hand weapons 90% (special). Scout (91-95%): the Warrior''s skills and Detect Ambush 88%, Wilderness Survival 84%, Land Navigation 78%, Tracking (Humanoids) 77%, Prowl 60%, Detect Concealment 55%. Officer (96-99%): everything above, Engineering and Scout skills included, and Horsemanship: General and War Chariot 90% (special). General (100%): the Officer''s skills. Any body of 100 or more works as field engineers (surveying, mapping, roads, bridges, walls, trenches, camps, demolition, catapults, ballistae, rams, siege towers); 1,000 or more can run a forge for hand weapons.', 'Sees well. Immune to S.D.C. weapons, ordinary fire and cold, toxins and disease; needs no air, water or food. M.D. weapons and magic attacks do half damage, M.D. explosions full. Regeneration: none on its own; it must choose to spend P.P.E., and each point spent restores 1 body M.D.C., as fast as its P.P.E. allows. The P.P.E. belongs to the spirit rather than the clay. Moulding armor: it pours its own P.P.E. into raw clay and fires it by magic at 1 P.P.E. per point of armor M.D.C., usually a single piece every couple of days; on anyone but a Terra-Cotta Warrior the armor is S.D.C., and a piece made for a comrade needs special fitting. Moulding clone warriors: with enough wet clay and a full P.P.E. pool it shapes a copy of itself for half its P.P.E.; the copy begins at half M.D.C. and is filled a day or two afterwards. Most keep 1-4 copies with them and one or two more hidden. One spirit can link up to 10 copies to move as one, and can jump between them, normally to the least damaged. An Officer stands 6 ft (1.8 m) or taller; a General is six inches taller than any other warrior and can take over any Terra-Cotta body in sight within 3000 ft (914.4 m), leaving his own empty. Killing one: body and armor must both reach zero before the spirit jumps; the shock leaves it senseless and unseen in limbo for 1D6 weeks, after which it enters any waiting copy at once or takes 2D6 days to build a fresh body. VULNERABILITIES: P.P.E. activation - it needs a couple of points to function; at 1 P.P.E. it slows and cannot move, and at 0 it is a rigid clay figure without M.D.C., thought or defense. Magic - anything that disrupts or drains P.P.E. cripples it, and at zero the spirit is stuck inside until 2 P.P.E. return. Psionics - full damage and full effect on mind and emotions; mind control comes easily but never lasts, and a spirit that leaves the body remembers itself and its task.', 'None', 'None', '5-6 ft (1.5 to 1.8 m)', '200-300 lbs (90 to 120 kg)', 'Presumed immortal', 'The 11th Hell of Rifts China (Shanxi) alone, apart from missions beyond it', 'Emperor Huang Di, the only master it is able to serve; its own comrades come next in its loyalty', NULL, NULL, 'A soldier of fired clay worn by the spirit of one of Huang Di''s dead troops and driven by P.P.E. It is hard to destroy, copies itself out of wet clay and moves from body to body, and its army also builds the Emperor''s roads and walls.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.51-53'),
('tiny-terra-cotta-warrior', 'Tiny Terra-Cotta Warrior', 'construct', 'rifts', 0, 'Anarchist (30%), Miscreant (60%) or Diabolic (10%)', '{"IQ":"1D6+9","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"2D6+1","PS":"2D6+3","PP":"2D6+6","PE":"2D6+3","PB":"3D6","Spd":"2D6+2"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6+6', '2D6+12', NULL, 'The book titles this block "Miniature Terra-Cotta Warrior"; the kind is also known as the Miniature Army. Race: an artificial body hosting a spirit of the dead. P.S. is Supernatural. Body M.D.C.: the book prints "half their P.P.E." and 1D6+6 is the equivalent roll of half of 2D6+12; it follows current P.P.E. Without ambient P.P.E. the M.D.C. is S.D.C. No armor M.D.C. is printed. P.P.E. recovery as the full-sized warriors: 1 point an hour at most. All are 4th to 6th level Soldiers. 95% are male, 5% female. Sent out in groups of 2D6+2 (four to fourteen), and now and then by the hundred.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4}', 'The book prints no bonuses for the tiny warriors.', '4th to 6th level Soldier. Prowl 80%, Detect Ambush 55%, Tracking 50%, Detect Concealment 45%, Land Navigation 40%.', 'Sees well, with nightvision 200 ft (61 m). Immune to S.D.C. weapons, ordinary fire and cold, poison and disease. M.D. weapons and magic attacks do half damage, explosions full. Regeneration works as it does for the full-sized warriors: P.P.E. held by the spirit is spent point for point to restore body M.D.C., and nothing heals unless it chooses. It moulds small clay copies of itself the same way the large ones do. Explosives: it has no training in modern demolitions, grenades or explosives and takes heavy penalties setting a timer or placing a charge, yet it cannot leave fireworks and bombs alone and goes on trying no matter how many times it blows itself up. VULNERABILITIES: Size - little danger hand to hand; although an M.D.C. being it can be lifted, pinned or trapped, even by a child with a pillow. P.P.E. activation - it needs a couple of points; at 1 P.P.E. it slows and cannot move, and at 0 it is a rigid bit of clay without M.D.C. or defense. Magic - anything that disrupts P.P.E. cripples it, and at zero the spirit is stuck until 2 P.P.E. return. Psionics - mind control works especially well, Hypnotic Suggestion and Mind Bleeder most of all; a spirit that leaves the body is free of the effect and recalls what took place.', 'None', 'None', '4-18 in (10-45 cm), typically 10 in (25 cm)', '8-16 lbs (3.6 to 7.2 kg)', 'Presumed immortal', 'The 11th Hell of Rifts China alone, apart from missions on that realm''s behalf', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A doll-sized clay soldier, the humiliating body Huang Di gave to troublemakers among his dead troops. It slips into supply dumps, armories and storerooms to wreck them, loves fire and explosions it has no skill with, and is weak and easily trapped in a straight fight.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.53');
INSERT INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES
('huan-shih', 'Huan Shih', NULL, 'Celestial Master of Mount Song', 'rifts', 'Taoist Immortal (the book prints no Race line)', '20th level Taoist Immortal, 11th level Mystic Martial Artist', 20, 'Scrupulous', '1,658 years', '5 ft (1.5 m)', '100 lbs (45 kg)', '{"IQ":27,"ME":25,"MA":25,"PS":17,"PP":19,"PE":15,"PB":13,"Spd":12}', NULL, NULL, 316, 290, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":9,"strike":7,"parry":12,"dodge":6,"pull":8,"roll":13}', 'The 316 M.D.C. applies in a mega-damage setting; where S.D.C. rules hold he instead has 156 Hit Points and 182 S.D.C. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts plus Boxing, eight hand to hand attacks a melee. Saves: +9 vs psionics and insanity, +7 vs magic, +10 vs poison, +34% vs coma/death. Charm/impress 70%. The book prints no Horror Factor, no I.S.P. and no Damage line.', '[{"name":"Language: American","pct":90},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":93},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":88},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":97},{"name":"Temple Lore: Begging","pct":63},{"name":"Temple Lore: Fasting","pct":87},{"name":"Temple Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":90},{"name":"Temple Lore: Meditation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing","pct":90}]', 'Mandarin is his native tongue (spoken, read and written, no percentage). Climbing is printed 90/80%. No percentage: Swimming; Ancient (Chi) Weapon Proficiency: Bamboo Staff.', 'Refinements of Immortality, named by the book without further numbers in this block: Unity of Chi (2nd refining), Eye Contact Divination (3rd), Funereal Cloud of Living Chi (4th), Yellow Animus of the Element of Earth (5th), Control Undead/Living Dead (6th), Sovereignty over Demons of the Yama Kings (7th), Immortal Child at the 8th refining (it brings Flight, Levitation and a Chi Spectral Form), and at the 9th the Power of Ubiquity, which allows 81 copies of himself. VULNERABILITIES: none are printed for him.', 'None. Martial Art Powers: Xian Tai Chi Chuan 12th level, Pao Chih 10th level.', 'Unknown', NULL, NULL, 'Seal of the Celestial Master: a block of solid iron that doubles as a magical throwing weapon. Stamped on paper it leaves the Cloud Character, and any Chinese demon seeing it must save against a Horror Factor (13 for Lesser Demons, 11 for Greater Demons, 8 for Demon Lords) or fall prostrate in submission. Stamped on metal it leaves the Yin Character, giving Chinese Demons -2 to strike or parry against the marked item. Hurled at a victim it brands the Yang Character on them: a Chinese Demon so marked can only be rid of it by carrying out one order given on the Celestial Master''s behalf, and one who refuses wears a red character that needs 4D6 days to fade. Gourd of Wind and Water: one effect a day, chosen from three. (a) A strong wind of 30-70 mph (48 to 112 km) blowing whichever way he likes for 3D6 minutes. (b) Heavy rain for 2D6 minutes. (c) A single Black Thunder Cloud over an area he names for as long as 2D4 minutes, throwing lightning bolts of 2D4x10 M.D. each out to 3000 ft (914 m); the cloud gives him four extra attacks every melee round, and its thunder carries as far as 3 miles (4.8 km).', NULL, 'Cheerful and unassuming. He never orders anyone; he drops a quiet suggestion and lets people volunteer. He has no patience for the infernal court, has destroyed Demon Lords and then simply walked out on the Yama Kings, and would much rather be back in his hermit''s hut.', 'Four iron servants, written by the book as Tieh Ku Sheh, Tieh Ku Kuan, Tien Ku Yu and Tien Ku Xi: animated iron statues 8 ft (2.4 m) tall, each housing an ancient warrior''s spirit. Approximate attributes for each: I.Q. 14, M.E. 15, M.A. 15, P.S. 27, P.P. 22, P.E. 25, P.B. 5, Spd 20; 120 M.D.C. Their blows: punch 4D6 M.D., power punch 1D6x10 (uses two attacks), kick 5D6, stomp 2D6. Every one carries the Seal of the Celestial Master on its chest, so a Chinese demon, ghost or undead it touches is shocked and stunned unless it saves on 12 or better (Greater Demons treat it as Horror Factor 9, Demon Lords are immune). Each can also fire a chi blast six times a day, no more often than every third melee round, doing 3D6 multiplied by the local Chi Environment to M.D.C. creatures. Their weakness is dragon fire breath, which does them double damage. Master Fu Qiu, an 11th level Taoist Immortal living at Zixu Temple, is his right hand and teaches roughly twenty advanced students; he gets no stat block. No fewer than eighteen more Taoist Immortals, Priests and Enlightened Scholars live in the neighbourhood.', NULL, 'A slight, ancient hermit, 5 ft tall, who was drafted against his wishes into leading Henan, the land of the 1st Kingdom of Hell. He guides by gentle hints rather than commands and has faced down the court of the Yama Kings. All he really wants is to go home to his hut on Mount Song.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.12-13'),
('wu-je-nao', 'Wu Je Nao', NULL, 'Abbot of the Shaolin Temple', 'rifts', 'White Dragon (Bai Long)', '13th level White Dragon, 22nd level Mystic Martial Artist', 13, 'Principled', '2,199 years', '5 ft, 4 in (1.65 m) in human form; over 280 ft (85.3 m) long as a dragon', '165 lbs (74 kg) in human form', '{"IQ":28,"ME":30,"MA":31,"PS":42,"PP":25,"PE":28,"PB":27,"Spd":80}', NULL, NULL, 5600, 2400, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":13,"initiative":11,"strike":11,"parry":13,"dodge":9,"pull":11,"roll":11}', 'P.S. 42 is Supernatural. Spd 80 is the running figure (56 mph/89.6 km); flying is Spd 220 (150 mph/240 km). Thirteen physical attacks a melee. Skilled in every Martial Art as a 10th level warrior would be. Saves: +8 vs psionics and insanity, +9 vs magic, +11 vs poison. The book prints no Horror Factor and no I.S.P.', '[{"name":"Language: American","pct":45},{"name":"Language: Dragonese/Elven","pct":98},{"name":"Basic and Advanced Math","pct":88},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":67},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Western","pct":88},{"name":"Temple Lore: Meditation","pct":92},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing","pct":90}]', 'Mandarin is the native tongue (spoken, read and written, no percentage). Dragonese/Elven is spoken only. Climbing is printed 90%/80%. No percentage: Swimming; every Ancient Weapon Proficiency and every Ancient (Chi) Weapon Proficiency.', 'Changes shape at will with no limit on how long a form is held; becomes invisible at will and sees invisible things; nightvision reaches 1000 ft (305 m). Heals 2D4x10 M.D. every minute. Cold and fire, including plasma and magical M.D. fire, do only half damage. Teleports itself with 92% success and crosses dimensions with 98%. Has a prehensile tail and can create 4 Shadow Dragons. VULNERABILITIES: none are printed.', 'No spell casting abilities. Martial Art Powers: Ba Gua Kungfu 9th level, Bok Pai Kungfu 7th level, Xian Pu Kung Kungfu 10th level, Gui Long Kungfu 22nd level (the highest of anyone anywhere), Hsien Hsia Kungfu 6th level, Mien-Ch''uan Kungfu 7th level, Pao Chih 10th level, She Shen Kungfu 10th level, Xian Tai Chi Chuan 10th level, Tong Lun Kungfu 7th level.', 'All Healing, Physical and Sensitive powers, though seldom used. No costs and no I.S.P. figure are printed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Humorless, exacting and orderly. As a teacher the abbot is merciless about finding and exploiting each student''s weak points.', 'The Shaolin Temple''s fighters: no fewer than 24 Mystic Martial Artists who have reached 12th level or better in a Martial Art Power, 300 more of 6th level or above, and 2,400 students ranked 1st through 5th level (roll 1D4+1). Said to have known Huan Shih centuries ago.', NULL, 'A white dragon who has spent the last sixty years in human shape running the Shaolin Temple and studying the martial arts. As a human the abbot is a trim, muscular, sharp-featured woman with loose long black hair and black eyes like mirrors; the true form is a white-scaled serpent more than 280 ft long covered in 400 moving spiked tendrils.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.14-15'),
('chu-chiang', 'Chu Chiang', NULL, '2nd Yama King, the Sleeping Yama King', 'rifts', 'Yama King (the book prints no Race line)', '15th level Chi Mage, 9th level Necromancer, 9th level Mystic Martial Artist', 15, 'Aberrant evil', '13,000 years (a Yama King for about two thousand of them)', 'typically 6 ft (1.8 m); grows or shrinks at will, to at most 100 ft (30.5 m)', 'around 300 lbs (135 kg) at human size', '{"IQ":16,"ME":12,"MA":11,"PS":45,"PP":19,"PE":27,"PB":20,"Spd":31}', NULL, NULL, 10500, 11000, 800, NULL, 18, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":6,"strike":8,"parry":3,"dodge":3,"pull":6,"roll":3}', 'P.S. 45 is Supernatural. Eight attacks a melee, and every use of magic costs two of them. Saves: +11 vs psionics and insanity, +11 vs magic. Charm/impress 70%. He stays out of direct combat with lesser beings unless trapped and actually being hurt; his minions do the fighting. No Damage line is printed. If his godhood is dissolved (see vulnerabilities) his M.D.C. is halved, P.P.E. and I.S.P. drop to zero and his P.S. stops being Supernatural.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Art","pct":96},{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":94},{"name":"Dance","pct":90},{"name":"Gardening","pct":94},{"name":"Go","pct":90},{"name":"Imitate Voices & Impersonation","pct":80},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":90},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Temple Meditation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing","pct":90},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98}]', 'By magic he speaks and understands every language, and he reads all forms of Chinese. Imitate Voices & Impersonation is printed 80%/60% and Climbing 90/80%. No percentage: Ancient (Chi) Weapon Proficiency: Bamboo Staff.', 'Sees invisible things and has nightvision to 400 ft (122 m); dimensional teleport succeeds 95% of the time; never needs sleep, rest, drink or food. Nothing S.D.C. hurts him, nor do man-made explosive or energy M.D. weapons, cold, fire, poison or disease; psionics, M.D. magic and man-made M.D. hand to hand weapons do half. He regrows 8D6 M.D.C. each melee round, twice that on ley lines or where negative energy gathers, and just 2D6 a round where positive chi or energy prevails. Manipulate Dragon Lines: he can speed a ley line''s energy up as high as Equinox level or slow it down, and bend a line toward or away from himself by altering its length by as much as 9 miles (14.4 km) (the book points to Rifts RPG p. 162-163). Summon and Command Demons: a demon he calls by name arrives at once and obeys; one unknown to him avoids the summons only by saving vs magic on 15 or better, and an unnamed demon resists an order only with a roll above his Horror Factor of 18. Metamorphosis: an instant change into any shape, dragons included, gaining the new shape''s natural abilities while keeping all his own. He can also copy the looks of a particular person he has seen; the infernals, undead and demons who serve him are completely fooled, but people who know the original well will probably see through it. Torturous Breath: an unseen gas exhaled through the nose covering a 40 ft (12.2 m) radius at up to 300 ft (91.5 m); those caught in it collapse inside two melee rounds (30 seconds) and stay unconscious 2D6+6 minutes. VULNERABILITIES: three legal weak points in his written Mandate. (1) Point of Correction - whoever shows him breaking the Mandate cannot be attacked by him directly, and he may not send infernals after that person, though he may still ask a mortal to do it. (2) Accusation of Neglect - a charge that is exact, with names and dates, lets the accuser give him orders as if an overseer sent by the Jade Emperor. (3) Dissolution of Godhood - proven in breach of three or more separate parts of the Mandate, with a channel open to the Jade Emperor''s Court, he is stripped of his divine powers (half M.D.C., zero P.P.E. and I.S.P., ordinary P.S., no special abilities) and led away in custody.', 'All Wizard Invocations, including the Spells of Legend: Blight of Ages (600), Doppleganger: Superior (1000), Sanctuary (1500), Warrior Horde (1100). Also all Necromancy spells and Temporal Magic. Demonic curses: all. Martial Art Powers: Ba Gua Kungfu 9th level, Hsien Hsia Kungfu 7th level, She Shen Kungfu 7th level, Hien-Hsueh Kungfu 9th level.', 'Master Psychic, 800 I.S.P.: Mind Block Auto-Defense, Object Read (6), Mask P.P.E. (4), Read Dimensional Portal (6), See Aura (6), Sense Time (2), Telepathy (4), and all Super Psionics.', NULL, NULL, 'Bing Chi Chui, the Ice Spider: a white house spider smaller than a coin with 1 Hit Point. The King draws a map in calligraphy marked with the symbols for the four compass points; set down on it, the spider permanently changes the weather of whatever spot on the map he picks (this is how Jingbo Lake became the Lake of Mirrored Ice). Killed, it returns with the next moon, unless cold or ice did the killing or its corpse is melted down in a vat of boiling silver.', NULL, 'Spoiled, lazy and withdrawn. He punishes whoever brings unwelcome news, so the court tells him only pleasant lies while the kingdom rots around him. The book leaves open that the neglect is an act.', 'His court at Harbin, none of it loyal (no numbers are printed for any of them). Hua Han the Chamberlain tells every Demon Lord the throne will be theirs and wants it for himself. Suan Tao, a Courtesan Demon and his consort under her Mandate, is clever, cruel and bored, and he has not looked at her in fifty years. Wang Bai the Court Artisan is the one being he cares to see; Wang Bai builds him torture devices as presents, tests them on workshop visitors, and privately hopes to lock the King into a pain machine. Harbin holds sixteen small palaces of Demon Lords, of which seven are described: (1) Lord Jing Bo of Jingbo Lake, the strongest, leading armies of demons suited to cold; (2) Shou Xing the Beast Demon, whose dungeon is The Butchery, served by Ox, Pig, Horse and Goat Demons; (3) Bai Meng, the Realm of the Famished, where Five Hundred Preta Ghosts serve its Lord, a female 9th level Yaksha known as the Lonely One who despises the King; (4) Fei Tieh, a winged Lord with hundreds of Gargoyles and Falcon Demons who hangs bodies on the red-hot walls; (5) Bai Yu, who keeps tracking demons at the Wudalianchi hunting fields and after a run-in with whom Xian Ya''s mentor died; (6) Gou Gou, a dog-shaped demon running a pack of dozens of dog demons; (7) Tu Mao, whose palace of medical torture punishes incompetent doctors. The city itself: iron walls as high as 3200 ft (975.3 m) that deal 1 M.D. to anything touching them, an inner palace wall that deals 1D6 M.D. a touch, and one gate watched by sixteen horned demon guards.', 'In effect his whole household: each servant has been turned against him or is scheming on their own account.', 'An ancient god-king, second of the Yama Kings, who rules the frozen 2nd Kingdom of Hell (Hanbing) from Harbin and has shut himself away behind its glowing walls. His authority rests on a Mandate from the Jade Emperor whose wording also gives his opponents exact legal ways to bind or unseat him.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.16-19'),
('xian-ya', 'Xian Ya', NULL, 'the Immortal Raven', 'rifts', 'winged D-Bee (the book prints no race name)', '10th level Cyber-Doc/Cyber-Engineer (not used for a very long time), 5th level Taoist Initiate, 8th level Mystic Martial Artist', 10, 'Principled', '483 years', '8 ft (2.4 m), with a 16 ft (4.9 m) wingspan', '1900 lbs (855 kg)', '{"IQ":31,"ME":17,"MA":14,"PS":20,"PP":27,"PE":30,"PB":22,"Spd":22}', 212, 68, NULL, 400, 138, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":7,"strike":5,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"pull":2,"roll":6}', 'Dodge rises to +10 while flying. On the M.D.C. line the book says she withstands 3 M.D. unarmored and may go into a fight wearing M.D. armor or under protective magic. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts. Saves: +8 vs psionics and insanity, +3 vs magic, +2 vs poison, +4% vs coma/death. Charm/impress 30%. No Horror Factor and no Damage line are printed.', '[{"name":"Language and Literacy: Mandarin","pct":76},{"name":"Language: American","pct":43},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":58},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":67},{"name":"Lore: Temple Meditation","pct":38},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":58}]', 'Mandarin is spoken, read and written at the one figure. From her old profession she may try nearly any cybernetic, mechanical or electronics repair at 88%. No percentage: Boxing.', 'Flight on wings spanning 16 ft (4.9 m), which is what lifts her dodge to +10 in the air. Unarmored she can take 3 M.D. and live. No other natural abilities are listed. VULNERABILITIES: none are printed.', 'Armor Bizarre (15), Armor of Ithan (10), Aura of Power (4), Befuddle (6), Blinding Flash (1), Call Lightning (15), Chromatic Protection (10), Cleanse (6), Deflect (10), Dessicate the Supernatural (50), Extinguish Fire (4), Globe of Daylight (2), Lantern Light (1), Magic Shield (6), Mystic Fulcrum (5), Manipulate Objects (2+), Mend the Broken (10+), See the Invisible (4), Sense Evil (2), Turn Dead (6). Martial Art Powers: Mien-Ch''uan Kungfu 8th level.', 'Full range of Healing Psionics. 138 I.S.P.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Considerate and careful, a quiet spiritual guide rather than a commander.', NULL, 'Demon Lord Bai Yu of Harbin; her mentor died following a clash with him.', 'An alien refugee who hid alone in the mountains for twenty years until temple chanting drew her back among people, where a Taoist mentor took her in; after his death she became the spiritual leader of Wuliang Temple on Mount Qian. She looks like an eight-foot angelic bird-woman with orange, yellow and gold feathers, talons on her limbs, enormous golden eyes and eight little tentacles inside her mouth.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.19-20'),
('qin-kuai', 'Qin Kuai', NULL, 'the Usurper, Viceroy of the 3rd Kingdom of Hell', 'rifts', 'damned soul, now a minor supernatural being (the book prints no Race line)', '7th level Chi Mage', 7, 'Diabolic evil', '1,232 years as a damned soul in the 3rd Yama King''s Hell', '5 ft, 4 in (1.6 m)', 'around 165 lbs (74.2 kg)', '{"IQ":18,"ME":17,"MA":17,"PS":18,"PP":12,"PE":11,"PB":8,"Spd":8}', NULL, NULL, 79, 106, NULL, NULL, 9, '{"attacks":2,"initiative":1}', 'P.S. 18 is Supernatural. Horror Factor 9 is for the human shape; as a rotting corpse it is 12. Per melee he gets two physical attacks, or three actions outside combat. Saves: +4 vs psionics and insanity, +3 vs magic, +1 vs psionic attack and possession. His own 79 M.D.C. dates from his death and promotion; for more he puts on M.D.C. armor (usually 100-200 M.D.C.), uses protective magic or climbs inside his living statue. No Damage line is printed.', '[{"name":"Language and Literacy: Chinese","pct":98},{"name":"Archaeology","pct":75},{"name":"Basic & Advanced Math","pct":90},{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":98},{"name":"Law","pct":75},{"name":"Military Etiquette","pct":80},{"name":"Forgery","pct":65},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":60},{"name":"Interrogation Techniques","pct":75},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":90},{"name":"Research","pct":85},{"name":"Surveillance Systems","pct":75},{"name":"Swimming","pct":95},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":90},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":90},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":88},{"name":"Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":68},{"name":"Bureaucracy & Administrative Organization","pct":98}]', 'Chinese is spoken, read and written at the one 98% figure.', 'Nightvision of 40 ft (12 m); he can show himself by night or day but keeps out of direct sunlight. Rotting Corpse form: the change is instant, while returning to human shape needs 2D6 melee rounds. As a corpse he can let loose a Stench of Putrification over a 20 ft (6.1 m) radius; anyone there who fails a save vs poison of 16 or better retches, giving up two melee attacks a round and taking -2 on every combat bonus. He mends one M.D.C. a melee round, and a body that is destroyed outright is whole again 48 hours later. VULNERABILITIES: physical attacks hurt him exactly as they would any of the dead or damned, and because he took the throne without a Mandate of his own he has no godlike powers at all.', 'None, except by reading scrolls written in Chinese or through a magic item. Demonic curses: none.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Royal Seal of the 3rd Yama King: a huge jade seal whose Cloud Character stamp makes a document official and its laws binding, and through which he gives orders to Lesser Demons, Greater Demons and even Demon Lords; no numbers. Ledger of Heavenly Correctness: an 1800-page book of protocol. An order or correction backed by a quotation from it cannot be refused by a Demon Lord; any lesser infernal (demon, goblin, ghost, undead, the dead or the damned) who hears so much as a brief passage takes 2D6 M.D.; and its characters, normally a phrase of four or more, can be branded into the skin of the damned to torment them for as long as a year. The 3rd Yama King''s Mandate of the Jade Emperor, with three conditions: (1) as long as it is in his hands, no infernal of the 3rd Kingdom will dare attack or lay a hand on him; (2) read aloud, it compels obedience from even the mightiest Demon Lord; (3) its characters written on a window, wall or door keep out every Demon Lord, lesser infernal, goblin, ghost and all the damned or dead.', NULL, 'Suspicious, treacherous and a bureaucrat to the bone. Weak in body, he governs through paperwork, his artifacts and the iron statue rather than by personal force, and he will not attempt the wider conquest his wife demands.', 'His wife Lady Wang and the brothers Feng Xiao and Feng Zhong, each with a living iron statue (separate entries). Thirteen Demon Lords sit in Hangzhou, with four entries described and no stat numbers: (1) the Demoness Seng Ka, once consort to Song Ti, with an army of Wasp Demons; her estate contains Hu Pao Spring and its two Yin Creatures, and the spring''s water adds +20% to pleasing a tea connoisseur and +20% to brewing healing, magical or ordinary potions and brews. (2) Nuan He, tormentor of the unfilial, holding more than 2 million dead and staffed by record-keeping demons. (3) Hsuan Ma of the Palace of the Forgers, who is raising a private army. (4) The lesser infernals he favors: Fox Faeries, Pig Demons, Ox-Head Demons, Headless Ones, Kinnaras, the Red Child and Ch''uan the Earth Hound, plus Kou Ching, whom he rarely orders about in person. Demon Lords of greater Zhejiang: Lon Mong of the Hanging Forest, a horse fancier with 12,000 demons (henchmen 50% Ma Tou Horse Demons, 25% Ox-Head Demons, 10% Monkey-Wolf, 5% Long-Armed Giants, 10% others) and a forest haunted by Preta, Kuei and Shen Mo ghosts; Shu Mo of Xi''Nan Jiang, first Lord of the Book Demons, who all bear the name Shu Mo and a brand on the forehead; and Yuan Shai of Wen Zhou, City of the Flayers, who refuses contact with Qin Kuai and keeps a dozen dungeons for prisoners and runaway slaves. Book Demon quick stats: an unusually intelligent Lesser Demon, average alignment Aberrant; every attribute 3D6 with +8 on I.Q., M.E. and P.S. (Supernatural); average M.D.C. 2D6x10+26; Horror Factor 10, or 15 for anyone who has mistreated books; five attacks per melee; nightvision 100 ft (30.5 m); regrows 1D6 M.D.C. a melee round. Skills: all languages by magic (spoken, read, written) 95%; Advanced and Basic Math 90%; 85% in Writing, Cryptology, Calligraphy, Research, Mythology, History, the Law and every Lore; Animal Husbandry and Holistic Medicine 80%; Find Contraband and Intelligence 75%; Radio: Basic and Operate Computers 70%; any four Mechanical or Science skills 60%. They have no psionics or magic and no special power except sensing censors, book burners and anyone who fears or hates books; they hoard and adore books and take them as bribes. They are ugly blue-skinned humanoids with slit eyes and green or yellow hair. Shu Mo''s other minions, maybe a hundred of each: Fox Faeries, Goat Demons, Shadow Goblins, and the Greater demons Yakshas and Shen Wu Warriors.', 'The Demon Lords under him are plotting his fall, and Seng Ka, the old king Song Ti''s consort, quietly seethes.', 'In life a treacherous official who had General Yue Fei killed; damned for it, he later seized the throne of the 3rd Kingdom of Hell (Zhejiang, seat at Hangzhou) once his iron likeness came to life, a position the book says was NOT gained through the Mandate of the Jade Emperor. He is a small man, 5 ft 4 in, who can also appear as a rotting corpse.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.20-25'),
('living-statue-of-qin-kuai', 'Living Statue of Qin Kuai', NULL, 'iron doppleganger of King Qin Kuai', 'rifts', 'living statue animated by Qin Kuai''s bond', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '8 ft (2.4 m)', '1000 lbs (450 kg)', '{"IQ":18,"ME":17,"MA":17,"PS":40,"PP":20,"PE":30,"PB":4,"Spd":20}', NULL, NULL, 890, NULL, NULL, NULL, 15, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":4,"strike":6,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"pull":2}', 'The book prints the attributes as Qin Kuai''s own apart from P.S. 40 (Supernatural), P.P. 20, P.E. 30, P.B. 4 and Spd 20, so I.Q. 18, M.E. 17 and M.A. 17 here are carried over from his block. (These printed figures do not follow the +15 P.S./+15 Spd rule the book gives for the family''s statues.) Eight physical attacks, 10 with Qin Kuai inside; his merging also adds +2 to every bonus. Saves: +2 vs psionics and insanity, +8 vs magic. Poison, disease and exhaustion do nothing to it. Damage is identical whether or not he occupies it. It thinks with his mind, so no alignment, level or P.P.E. is printed.', NULL, NULL, 'Knows on sight anybody who once spat on the statue, and their descendants: the odds of having spitters for ancestors are 01-66% for someone whose descent is purely Chinese and 33% for someone half-Chinese. Those who insult or defy Qin Kuai today get the same punishment. It regrows 4D6 M.D.C. a melee round, twice that at ley lines or sites of negative energy. Whenever Qin Kuai comes under attack it teleports to stand beside him, and he can merge into it. Destroyed, it spits him out and has reformed 48 hours later. S.D.C. weapons and M.D. fire cannot harm it. VULNERABILITIES: M.D. weapons and cold inflict their normal damage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'No will of its own: it shares Qin Kuai''s thoughts and serves as his torturer, seizing victims and breaking them by raw strength.', 'Qin Kuai, whose second body it is.', NULL, 'The iron likeness of Qin Kuai from his mausoleum, spat on by generations of visitors and brought to life by his fury. It is a huge, crude, naked metal copy of the man that never stops sweating stale mucus.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.22'),
('lady-wang', 'Lady Wang', NULL, 'wife of Qin Kuai', 'rifts', 'the book prints no Race line (Quick Stats for the woman herself, not her statue)', NULL, NULL, 'Diabolic', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":15,"ME":9,"MA":10,"PS":9,"PP":11,"PE":12,"PB":10,"Spd":8}', 41, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Quick Stats only: the book prints no level, attacks per melee, bonuses, P.P.E. or damage for her.', '[{"name":"Cooking","pct":50}]', 'Courtly skills, every one at 80%: Chinese (spoken, read, written), Basic Math, Calligraphy, Dance, Floral Arrangement, Poetry and Lore: Religion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Cruel and fixated on rank. The spitting shames her even more than it does her husband, and she treats him with open contempt for refusing to conquer the rest of China''s Hells and crown the two of them Emperor and Empress.', 'Qin Kuai, her husband, and her own living statue, which she uses as a bodyguard.', NULL, 'The status-obsessed wife of Qin Kuai, consort to the usurper of the 3rd Kingdom of Hell. The book gives both her own Quick Stats and a separate living iron statue of her.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.22-23'),
('living-statue-of-lady-wang', 'Living Statue of Lady Wang', NULL, 'iron likeness of Lady Wang', 'rifts', 'living statue animated by Lady Wang''s bond', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '6 ft (1.8 m)', '600 lbs (270 kg)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 540, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":6,"strike":2,"parry":4,"dodge":4}', 'No attribute numbers are printed. The rule given is that the statue uses Lady Wang''s attributes with +15 to P.S., which becomes Supernatural, and +15 to Spd. Saves: +4 vs psionics and insanity, +4 vs magic. Possession cannot touch her while she is inside it. The M.D.C., attacks and bonuses shown are for the statue with Lady Wang in it; animated without her, each is halved, rounding down.', NULL, NULL, 'Recognizes at once anyone who spat on the statue, or whose forebears did. Regrows 3D6 M.D.C. a melee round, twice that at ley lines or sites of negative energy. S.D.C. weapons and M.D. fire cannot harm it. VULNERABILITIES: cold and all other M.D. weapons inflict normal damage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Lady Wang gets no enjoyment from wearing it and leaves it to act as her bodyguard.', 'Lady Wang.', NULL, 'A crude, oversized, naked metal copy of Lady Wang that sweats stale mucus, one of the four iron figures from Qin Kuai''s mausoleum that came alive.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.23'),
('feng-xiao', 'Feng Xiao', NULL, 'underling of Qin Kuai, elder brother of Feng Zhong', 'rifts', 'the book prints no Race line (Quick Stats for the man himself, not his statue)', NULL, NULL, 'Miscreant', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":15,"ME":12,"MA":13,"PS":14,"PP":10,"PE":10,"PB":9,"Spd":11}', 38, 20, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Quick Stats only: the book prints no level, attacks per melee, bonuses, P.P.E. or damage for him.', '[]', 'The same courtly skills as Lady Wang (Chinese spoken, read and written, Basic Math, Calligraphy, Dance, Floral Arrangement, Poetry, Lore: Religion), but at 70%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A venal, cowardly flatterer. He makes up rumors and lies to excuse wicked acts, and when he tires of grovelling he takes it out on his younger brother.', 'Qin Kuai, his master; his brother Feng Zhong; his own living statue.', NULL, 'The elder of the two Feng brothers who served Qin Kuai in life and serve him still in the 3rd Kingdom of Hell. The book gives him Quick Stats and a separate living iron statue.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.23'),
('living-statue-of-feng-xiao', 'Living Statue of Feng Xiao', NULL, 'iron likeness of Feng Xiao', 'rifts', 'living statue animated by Feng Xiao''s bond', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '8 ft (2.4 m)', '900 lbs (405 kg)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 640, NULL, NULL, NULL, 14, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":5,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"disarm":2,"pull":2}', 'No attribute numbers are printed. The rule given is that the statue uses Feng Xiao''s attributes with +15 to P.S., which becomes Supernatural, and +15 to Spd. Saves: +4 vs psionic attack and insanity, +4 vs magic. Possession cannot touch him while he is inside it. The M.D.C., attacks and bonuses shown are for the statue with Feng Xiao in it; animated without him, each is halved, rounding down.', NULL, NULL, 'Recognizes at once anyone who spat on the statue, or whose forebears did. Regrows 3D6 M.D.C. a melee round, twice that at ley lines or sites of negative energy. S.D.C. weapons and M.D. fire cannot harm it. VULNERABILITIES: cold and M.D. weapons inflict normal damage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Feng Xiao.', NULL, 'A crude naked metal copy of Feng Xiao that sweats stale mucus, one of the four iron figures from Qin Kuai''s mausoleum that came alive.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.23'),
('feng-zhong', 'Feng Zhong', NULL, 'underling of Qin Kuai, younger brother of Feng Xiao', 'rifts', 'the book prints no Race line (Quick Stats for the man himself, not his statue)', NULL, NULL, 'Miscreant', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":17,"ME":8,"MA":9,"PS":12,"PP":11,"PE":9,"PB":9,"Spd":14}', 38, 20, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Quick Stats only: the book prints no level, attacks per melee, bonuses, P.P.E. or damage for him.', '[]', 'The same courtly skills as Lady Wang (Chinese spoken, read and written, Basic Math, Calligraphy, Dance, Floral Arrangement, Poetry, Lore: Religion), but at 55%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Neurotic and bullied. He cringes before those above him, is sadistic to those below, and loves being inside his iron statue.', 'Qin Kuai, his master; his brother Feng Xiao; his own living statue.', NULL, 'The younger of the two Feng brothers who serve Qin Kuai in the 3rd Kingdom of Hell, forever pushed around by his elder brother. The book gives him Quick Stats and a separate living iron statue.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.23'),
('living-statue-of-feng-zhong', 'Living Statue of Feng Zhong', NULL, 'iron likeness of Feng Zhong', 'rifts', 'living statue animated by Feng Zhong''s bond', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '8 ft (2.4 m)', '900 lbs (405 kg)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 640, NULL, NULL, NULL, 14, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":6,"strike":4,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"pull":2}', 'No attribute numbers are printed. The rule given is that the statue uses Feng Zhong''s attributes with +15 to P.S., which becomes Supernatural, and +15 to Spd. Saves: +4 vs psionic attack and insanity, +2 vs magic. Possession cannot touch him while he is inside it. The M.D.C., attacks and bonuses shown are for the statue with Feng Zhong in it; animated without him, each is halved, rounding down.', NULL, NULL, 'Recognizes at once anyone who spat on the statue, or whose forebears did. Regrows 3D6 M.D.C. a melee round, twice that at ley lines or sites of negative energy. S.D.C. weapons and M.D. fire cannot harm it. VULNERABILITIES: cold and M.D. weapons inflict normal damage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Feng Zhong loves living inside it.', 'Feng Zhong.', NULL, 'A crude naked metal figure that sweats stale mucus and looks little like Feng Zhong, being a reworked version of his brother''s statue. It is one of the four iron figures from Qin Kuai''s mausoleum that came alive.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.23-24'),
('wu-kuan', 'Wu Kuan', NULL, '4th Yama King (Judge Wu Kuan Wang), ruler of Fujian Province, the 4th Kingdom of Hell', 'rifts', 'Yama King, a god (the book prints no Race line)', '25th level Enlightened Scholar, 10th level Necromancer, 11th level Mystic Martial Artist', 25, 'Aberrant evil (almost perfectly Aberrant)', '9,600 years; a Yama King for 1,450 of them', '5 ft 10 in (1.78 m) normally; grows or shrinks at will', 'about 175 lbs (78.7 kg)', '{"IQ":27,"ME":29,"MA":20,"PS":32,"PP":24,"PE":30,"PB":26,"Spd":21}', NULL, NULL, 11000, 6100, 1200, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":2,"strike":5,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"pull":2,"roll":2}', 'P.S. 32 is Supernatural. The six attacks are physical ones; every spell cast uses up two of them. Saves: +10 vs magic, +7 vs insanity and psionics; possession cannot affect him. 80% to charm/impress and 60% to evoke trust or intimidation. No Damage line is printed for him.', '[{"name":"Literacy: Chinese (all)","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Russian","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Korean","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Japanese","pct":98},{"name":"Art","pct":98},{"name":"Astronomy","pct":98},{"name":"Astrology","pct":98},{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":98},{"name":"Dance","pct":98},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":98},{"name":"History: China","pct":98},{"name":"Law","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Religion","pct":98},{"name":"Research","pct":98},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":75},{"name":"Go","pct":75},{"name":"Interrogation Techniques","pct":75},{"name":"Poetry","pct":75},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":75},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":75},{"name":"Seduction","pct":75},{"name":"Writing","pct":75}]', 'Speaks and understands every language by magic. Every Ancient (Chi) Weapon Proficiency, each at 8th level. The 98% list also prints a stray word ''Basic'' after Tea Appreciation with no skill name attached; it is not stored as a skill.', 'Sees invisible things and has nightvision out to 2000 ft (610 m). Dimensional teleport succeeds 90% of the time. Without effort he is aware of, and can judge, every ley line (dragon line) inside 100 miles (160 km). S.D.C. weapons, cold, fire, poison and disease cannot hurt him at all, while psionics, M.D. magic and man-made M.D. weapons do only half damage. He heals 6D6 M.D.C. each melee round, twice that at places of negative energy or on a ley line, and just 2D6 where positive energy or chi prevails. Food, drink, sleep and rest are unnecessary, though fine food and drink please him. Summon and Command Demons: any demon whose name he knows must appear at once and obey; a demon he does not know needs 15 or better to save against the magical summoning, and one he cannot name may refuse an order only by rolling above his Horror Factor of 17 (in his presence most obey anyway). Metamorphosis: takes any shape instantly, a dragon included, acquiring that shape''s natural abilities and keeping all his own; he can also copy a specific individual he has seen, perfectly for demons, undead and infernals who serve him, though people who know another original well will spot the fake. Temporal Freeze (special): at will he halts time anywhere inside his domain so that he alone can move, for up to 60 minutes (rarely longer than a few), six times in any 24 hours. VULNERABILITIES: Millennium Tree weapons do five times their usual damage to him. He keeps his Mandate of the Jade Emperor flawlessly, so it holds no threat; the one thing he need fear is facing the Jade Emperor''s power directly.', 'All Necromancy magic, and every spell Invocation of levels 1-10. Demonic curses: all. Martial Art Powers: Ba Gua Kungfu 11th level, Pao Chih 11th level, Tong Lun Kungfu 9th level.', 'I.S.P. 1200, no costs printed. Every Sensitive power and the Mind Bleeder powers; Super: Telemechanics, Psychic Omni-Sight, Mind Wipe, Group Trance, Group Mind Block and Mind Block Auto-Defense; the book adds that he may have others nobody knows of.', NULL, NULL, 'The Nine Treasure and Cloud Radiance Throne: a seat cut from a single block of enchanted white jade and inscribed with Cloud Characters. Its occupant sees the world as if from heaven and can fix on any event anywhere on Rifts Earth. He watches only his own kingdom with it. No Yama King artifact is more envied. The book prints no M.D.C., damage or range for it.', NULL, 'Unfailingly courteous, exacting and legalistic. He believes flawless Confucian administration will see him named Emperor, and he binds anyone who deals with him in written contracts, which is why his fellow Yama Kings keep their distance.', 'Tens of thousands of demons inhabit Fujian, all of them obedient and individually accounted for; the book names none and gives no closer count. PLACES AND ITEMS OF HIS PROVINCE, NOT HIS POSSESSIONS (p.27-28): the Orthodox Oneness Temple is kept by Xian Tan (Immortal Cinnabar), an Immortal Taoist attended by the Yin Tigers Shao Huan and Shao Tuan (no numbers printed), and she lends its artifacts out for special missions. (1) Peach-Wood Stick for Beating Ghosts: lets its holder seize intangible spirits and hurt ghosts, vampires, undead and the damned in full; it deals neither S.D.C. nor M.D.C., but each blow hurts like 6D6 points of damage and the target must save vs Horror Factor (no number printed) or stand frozen with terror. (2) Female and Male Swords for Slaying Demons with the Three Virtuous Ways: a matched pair for two fighters working side by side, the dark green Yin blade for a woman and the golden Yang blade for a man; each does 3D6+12 M.D. to demons, undead and evil supernatural beings, spirits and gods included. (3) Da Ling Sheng (Soul Bells): five little bells of black bronze strung on a necklace of jade beads; ringing them takes 14 or better on a D20 plus P.P. bonus, and then every ghost, goblin, damned or dead thing and creature of chaos that can hear them, out to 3000 ft (914 m), runs; any made to remain bleeds at the ears and falls unconscious within 1D6 melee rounds. (4) Refining Elixir well of Mount Gezao, where four ley lines meet: magic worked there goes wrong 01-33% of the time. A cursed object left in the water 24 hours is cleansed. A cursed person must save vs magical cold every hour (12 needed, at -1 for each two hours spent in the water) and after 12 hours must also roll under half their M.E. (M.E. 15 counts as 7); under 5% endure all 24 hours. Drunk, the water settles minor stomach trouble; at the full moon it sobers the drunk and flushes poison; a drinker who then sleeps within 1000 ft (305 m) wakes clear-headed with +10% on all skills for 1D6 days. Carried away it has no magic but keeps cool and fresh for as long as six months.', 'None named. The other Yama Kings avoid him.', 'The judge-king of Fujian, a god of order, law and paperwork who rules his Hell with complete precision. On state occasions he shows the blackened skeleton of a Yama King; otherwise he looks like a good-looking Asian man, black-haired and rigidly upright, robed in silk or in garments of office.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.25-27'),
('yen-lo', 'Yen Lo', NULL, '5th Yama King, ruler of Guangdong Province, the 5th Kingdom of Hell', 'rifts', 'Yama King, a god (the book prints no Race line)', '13th level Scholar, 12th level Scientist (equivalent to the Rogue Scientist O.C.C.), 8th level Ley Line Walker, 7th level Necromancer', 13, 'Anarchist', '13,000 years; a Yama King for about 2,000 of them', '6 ft (1.8 m) normally; can grow as tall as 200 ft (61 m) or shrink', 'about 300 lbs (135 kg)', '{"IQ":27,"ME":23,"MA":17,"PS":31,"PP":26,"PE":29,"PB":13,"Spd":22}', NULL, NULL, 6250, 5800, 500, NULL, 11, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":5,"strike":8,"parry":6,"dodge":6,"pull":4,"roll":3}', 'P.S. 31 is Supernatural. Eight attacks a melee; any use of magic spends two of them. Saves: +9 vs Horror Factor, poison and magic, +5 vs insanity and psionics; possession cannot affect him. No Damage line is printed for him. He fights in person only when trapped with neither an escape nor a way to talk himself clear.', '[{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":95},{"name":"Basic & Advanced Mathematics","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Hacking","pct":60},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Programming","pct":90},{"name":"Computer Repair","pct":80},{"name":"Dance","pct":90},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Flute","pct":90},{"name":"Electrical Engineer","pct":95},{"name":"Electrical Generation","pct":95},{"name":"Field Armorer","pct":75},{"name":"Jury-Rig","pct":80},{"name":"Law","pct":95},{"name":"Temple Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98},{"name":"Mechanical Engineer","pct":95},{"name":"Automotive Mechanics","pct":90},{"name":"Mining","pct":70},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Scramblers","pct":95},{"name":"Surveillance Systems","pct":90},{"name":"TV/Video","pct":90},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":90},{"name":"Robot Mechanics","pct":90},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Weapons Engineer","pct":90},{"name":"Writing","pct":75}]', 'Speaks and understands every language by magic; reads Chinese (no percentage printed).', 'Sees invisible things and has nightvision out to 1000 ft (305 m). Dimensional teleport succeeds 90% of the time. S.D.C. weapons, cold, fire, poison and disease cannot hurt him; man-made M.D. weapons do half damage, but psionics and M.D. magic hurt him in full. He heals 1D4x10 M.D.C. each melee round, twice that at places of negative energy or on a ley line, and just 2D6 where positive energy or chi prevails. Food, drink, sleep and rest are unnecessary, though he likes good food and drink. Summon and Command Demons: any demon whose name he knows must appear at once and obey; a demon he does not know needs 15 or better to save against the magical summoning, and one he cannot name may refuse an order only by rolling above his Horror Factor of 11. VULNERABILITIES: he underwent the Ritual of Reversion and regards himself as free of his Mandate of the Jade Emperor. Psionics and magic do full damage and most man-made M.D. weapons half. Unfamiliar or alien technology distracts him, and his compulsion to collect devices and knowledge gives others a lever to steer him.', 'All Necromancy magic, and every spell Invocation; of the Spells of Legend he knows only Hivemind. Demonic curses: all. Martial Art Powers: none.', 'Master Psychic, I.S.P. 500. Telepathy (4), Sense Time (2), See Aura (6), Mask P.P.E. (4), Object Read (6), Mind Block Auto-Defense, and every Super Psionic power.', NULL, NULL, 'Bead strings of Tu Feng (Black Bees): on his order the bees become small beads of black stone threaded on a string. He wears one string of 300 beads and carries one or two more of 40+4D10 beads apiece. He may hand a single bee to someone for a quick message, or lend an entire spare string (40+4D10 bees) set to obey whoever carries it. The bees'' own numbers are under allies.', NULL, 'Good-humoured, driven and absorbed in invention. He seldom leaves his research complexes and treats any battle as a field trial for whatever his workshops have built.', 'Guangdong fields a modern army of roughly 2,000 officers, 40,000 technicians and 85,000 soldiers, of whom 17,000 are RPA specialists and 5,000 are pilots (p.29). TU FENG (BLACK BEES), p.30: glittering black bumblebees as big as a fist that share one hive mind; good as couriers and attackers, poor as spies or scouts. A bee can memorise by magic a message of as many as 500 words and repeat it exactly, and has two pouches for loose material, each holding 2 kilos (4 pounds). Alignment not printed; gender Female Neuter. I.Q. 5, M.A. 4, M.E. 8, P.S. 4 (Supernatural), P.P. 17, P.E. 5, P.B. 9, Spd 88 flying (60 mph/96 km). M.D.C. 7+1D6 per bee. Horror Factor 9 for a single bee, 12 for a dozen, 14 for a swarm of up to 100, 16 for a big swarm in the hundreds. Fire, cold and S.D.C. weapons do nothing; psionics, magic and M.D. weapons do normal damage; heals 1 M.D.C. a melee round, 2 at negative-energy places or on ley lines; a bee at zero M.D.C. is destroyed. Per melee: two bites at 1D4 M.D. apiece, or a single sting for 1D8 plus Paralyzing Poison (the book prints neither a unit for the sting nor a save or duration for the paralysis). +10 dodge, +5 strike and parry, +5 vs mind control, +4 vs psionic attack, +2 vs magic. NEVER-DYING SERVANTS, p.30-31: by a Soul Deal, humans who swear themselves to Yen Lo (officers, scientists, industrialists, administrators) rise after death as wild, unkempt figures with white-streaked hair and blank white eyes, keeping the attributes they had alive with these changes. Gains: P.S. +1D6 and now Supernatural; P.E. +1D4; Hit Points plus S.D.C. from life turn into M.D.C. with 6D6+6 more added; heals 1D6 M.D.C. a minute; one extra attack a melee; +4 vs possession, +4 vs Horror Factor, +2 vs magic; disease cannot touch them, poison and cold do half; they last 500 years as undead unless killed. Losses: I.Q. -2, M.A. -1D6, M.E. -1D4, and only four returns from death before Yen Lo loses them for good. Each rolls a D20 Save vs Undeath: 11-20 means no flaw; 01-10 means one flaw chosen by 1D6: 1 = sunlight blinds it and halves its M.D.C., P.S. and bonuses; 2 = mazes bewilder it and it is drawn to ley lines; 3 = positive Chi does it double damage and it cannot regenerate at positive places; 4 = rain or running water burns it, 2D6 M.D. each melee round in rain or 1D6 to 2D6 M.D. from each blast of water; 5 = it craves human flesh or blood and must feed once every 72 hours at least; 6 = it cannot touch silver, and a silver weapon does twice its S.D.C. damage as M.D. (a 1D6 S.D.C. silver dagger does 2D6 M.D.). Pien Cheng, Tai Shan Chun and Tu Shis the 9th Yama King also make such servants.', 'None named in his entry.', 'The inventor among the Yama Kings, who has rebuilt Guangdong as a computerised, industrial Hell and tinkers with ordinary and magical machines alike, though not Techno-Wizardry. He gave up the skeletal look of his kind and appears as a tall, lean man with Han Chinese features, very pale skin, green eyes and unruly red hair.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.29-31'),
('pien-cheng', 'Pien Cheng', NULL, '6th Yama King (Pien Cheng Wang), the Chairman; ruler of Shandong Province, the 6th Kingdom of Hell', 'rifts', 'Yama King, now a bodiless spirit that possesses human hosts (the book prints no Race line)', '15th level Chi Mage, 11th level Necromancer, 9th level Mystic Martial Artist', 15, 'Miscreant evil', '47,000 years; a Yama King for 1,460 of them', 'Human-sized; the book calls his size irrelevant because he has no body of his own', NULL, '{"IQ":26,"ME":31,"MA":22,"PS":27,"PP":23,"PE":17,"PB":18,"Spd":80}', NULL, NULL, 250, 5600, 390, NULL, 12, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":10,"strike":5,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"pull":4,"roll":4}', 'The attributes are those of whatever body he is possessing; the host takes on these figures. P.S. 27 is Supernatural; Spd 80 is roughly 55 mph (88 km). The stored M.D.C. of 250 is ADDED to the mortal body he occupies; he has 1,850 M.D.C. in his present spirit form and had 6,700 in his former god-like form. Horror Factor is printed as Horror/Awe Factor. Always male. Per melee: five psionic or physical attacks, or two spells. The +5 strike is for non-physical attacks. Saves: +8 vs Horror Factor and illusions, +8 vs insanity and psionics, +4 vs magic; mind control and possession cannot affect him. He strongly avoids personal combat.', '[{"name":"Anthropology","pct":95},{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":95},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":98},{"name":"Law (human)","pct":98},{"name":"Temple Lore: Sociology","pct":85},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":90},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":98},{"name":"Temple Lore: Meditation","pct":98},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":90},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":85},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":90},{"name":"Climbing","pct":90},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":60},{"name":"Prowl","pct":55},{"name":"Swimming","pct":90}]', 'Speaks and understands every language by magic; reads Chinese (no percentage printed). Every other Lore at 98%. Climbing is printed 90/80%. Whoever he possesses performs these skills.', 'Sees invisible things and has nightvision out to 1000 ft (305 m). Dimensional teleport succeeds 80% of the time. S.D.C. weapons, cold, fire, poison and disease cannot hurt him, and psionics, M.D. magic and man-made M.D. weapons do half damage. Whatever form he is in he heals 5D6 M.D.C. each melee round, twice that at places of negative energy or on a ley line, and just 2D6 where positive energy or chi prevails. As a spirit he needs no food, drink, sleep or rest; in a human host he gets by on a small part of what a person normally requires. Possess Living Human: he enters a host gently, the host drifting into sleep and recalling nothing afterwards. Summon and Command Demons: any demon whose name he knows must appear at once and obey; a demon he does not know needs 15 or better to save against the magical summoning, and one he cannot name may refuse an order only by rolling above his Horror Factor. Spirit Wrack (special): a psychic assault; a target who fails to save vs psionics is filled with doubt about their own name, past and purpose, or else he can burn away 4D10 (also printed 1D4x10) of the target''s I.S.P. every melee round. VULNERABILITIES: his Mandate of the Jade Emperor still binds him, but lacking a body he has no Point of Correction to dread. Psionic: a group of other powerful psychics acting together might overpower his mind. Magical: a Circle of Summoning made for him could be used to destroy him, though that takes enormous power and the mystic consent of the Jade Emperor''s Heavenly Court.', 'All Necromancy magic, and every spell Invocation other than the Spells of Legend. Demonic curses: all. Martial Art Powers: none.', 'Master Psychic, I.S.P. 390, able to run as many as three powers at once. Every Super, Sensitive, Physical and Healing power; no costs printed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Quiet, modest in manner and nameless by choice; he governs as an idea more than a person. He slips into living hosts without harming them and speaks through them as Chairman Cheng.', 'The People''s Army, the Cadres and the Red Guard of Shandong, forces he has purged and levelled, Demon Lords among them. His Never-Dying Servants (rules under Yen Lo) return younger and more idealistic, at half the usual penalties, yet wearier each time (p.36). PA''EN MO, Demon Overlord of the Land of the Locusts (p.36): the last Demon Lord left in Shandong and openly defiant of Pien Cheng; he has divided his body among millions of locusts and wrecks harvests when he pleases. The expectation is that he will be tracked down, bound and re-educated. The book prints no alignment, attributes or M.D.C. for him.', 'The Yama Kings who destroyed him after his failed bid to be Emperor; Pa''en Mo defies him. No Enemies line is printed.', 'Once the strongest of the Yama Kings, he was destroyed after reaching for the Emperor''s seat and came back without a body, as the faceless Chairman of a Perpetual Revolution in Shandong. He is seen only inside a human host or as a spirit, when he shows only the silhouette of an unremarkable Chinese citizen, most often wearing the Red Guard hat, trousers and shirt-jacket.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.34-36'),
('tai-shan-chun', 'Tai Shan Chun', NULL, 'Demon Regent of the 7th Kingdom of Hell, ruler of Hubei Province (a Demon Overlord, not officially a Yama King)', 'rifts', 'Demon Overlord (the book prints no Race line)', '23rd level Demon Overlord, 9th level Enlightened Scholar', 23, 'Aberrant evil', '87,600 years; the book prints "Yama King for just 359 years"', '25 ft (7.6 m); usually shows himself at about a third of that, 8 ft (2.4 m)', 'three tons', '{"IQ":30,"ME":26,"MA":22,"PS":42,"PP":20,"PE":25,"PB":17,"Spd":22}', NULL, NULL, 4700, 1300, 160, NULL, 16, '{"attacks":10,"initiative":6,"strike":6,"parry":7,"dodge":2,"disarm":4}', 'P.S. 42 is Supernatural. Male. Per melee: 10 physical attacks, or three magical ones. +8 to entangle. Saves: +7 vs Horror Factor, +4 vs mind control, +1 vs every kind of magic; possession and illusions cannot affect him. The book says these come on top of probable attribute bonuses. I.S.P. 160 appears only inside the Psionics line. An expert Demon Wrestler (entangle, pin, crush/squeeze) who favours magic and his natural abilities, sometimes psionics or a giant-sized sword for which no numbers are printed.', '[{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":98},{"name":"Detect Ambush","pct":85},{"name":"Detect Concealment","pct":80},{"name":"Interrogation Techniques","pct":90},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Temple Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":98},{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":90},{"name":"Dance","pct":90},{"name":"Dowsing","pct":90},{"name":"Gemology","pct":90},{"name":"History: China","pct":90},{"name":"Military Etiquette","pct":95},{"name":"Navigation","pct":95},{"name":"Recognize Weapon Quality","pct":95},{"name":"Seduction","pct":65},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":75}]', 'Speaks and understands every language by magic; reads Chinese (no percentage printed). Every other Lore at 70%. Every Ancient (Chi) Weapon Proficiency, with no level printed.', 'Sharp eyesight that pierces magical darkness and sees invisible things, with nightvision out to 3000 ft (914 m). He does not breathe and can stay in a vacuum without limit. Dimensional teleport succeeds 80% of the time. Disease, possession, ordinary heat and cold and S.D.C. weapons do nothing to him, with two exceptions: bone or silver weapons do their normal S.D.C. figure as M.D., and Mega-Damage heat or cold hurts him in full. Poison has half its effect for half as long. He heals 1D4x10 M.D.C. each melee round, twice that at places of negative energy or on a ley line, and just 2 M.D.C. a round where positive energy or chi prevails. Summon and Command Demons: any demon whose name he knows must appear at once and obey; a demon he does not know needs 15 or better to save against the magical summoning, and one he cannot name may refuse an order only by rolling above his Horror Factor. Metamorphosis: he takes most shapes; an animal shape brings its natural abilities, while a mystical shape such as a dragon may not bring that creature''s powers. Change Size at Will (special): anything between 1 ft (0.3 m) and 25 ft (7.6 m). VULNERABILITIES: psionics and magic get no special resistance from him and do full damage whenever he fails a save. He works under a special supplement to his predecessor''s Mandate of the Jade Emperor; being a Demon Overlord and no Yama King, he need only fulfil it as well as he can, so it threatens him little.', 'All spell invocations of levels 7-15, plus the Spells of Legend Doppleganger Superior (1000), Metropolis (1600) and Sanctuary (1500). Demonic curses: all. Martial Art Powers: none.', 'Master Psychic, I.S.P. 160. Every Super and Physical power, plus Telepathy (4).', NULL, NULL, 'The Wind-Fire Pagoda: a magical flying war artifact kept in the innermost courtyard of his palace. It has eight storeys, every one high enough for a Demon Lord to stand in, lifts off and flies at Spd 110 (printed as 110/75 mph/120 km), and carries up to 100 armed demons. No M.D.C. or weapon damage is printed. Rumour says he is bargaining with the 5th Yama Kingdom for M.D. weapons to turn it into a flying fortress.', NULL, 'Forceful, quick-witted and fond of a brawl; his efforts to avoid a fight are never wholehearted. He takes in deserters from some of the other Yama Kings and builds alliances with renegade Taoists and Gargoyles.', 'An Inner Chamber of 14 Demon Overlords, a House of Demon Lords numbering more than 500, and upward of four million demons. He also makes Never-Dying Servants (rules under Yen Lo). Named Demon Lords of his realm, none with printed numbers (p.40): Fang Changyu, Demon Lady of the Renao Diyu, Shang Chengdao and Guo Yi. Chi Chou Lu, Ast-Oth and Zhua Zhao have rows of their own. Creatures printed in Fang Changyu''s entry (p.40): SHIH LANG (JACKAL WOLVES), demonic jackal wolves weighing over 250 pounds (112.5 kg) that run in packs of 30 or 40 and torment their prey. Alignment Aberrant. I.Q. 12, M.E. 13, M.A. 14, P.S. 24 (Supernatural), P.P. 21, P.E. 22, P.B. 9, Spd 58 (40 mph/64 km). M.D.C. 1D6x10+44; P.P.E. 2D6x10+12; 4 ft (1.2 m) at the shoulder; magic is all Air Elemental spells of levels 1-3. FENG SHIH (DEMON BOARS), their rivals, boars of as much as 1,750 pounds (787.5 kg) found in groups of 8-12 and known for frightening calls and choruses. Alignment Diabolic. I.Q. 8, M.E. 10, M.A. 8, P.S. 32 (Supernatural), P.P. 15, P.E. 24, P.B. 3, Spd 58 (40 mph/64 km). M.D.C. 1D6x10+66; Horror Factor 13 from their sound alone; P.P.E. 2D6x10; 4 ft (1.2 m) at the shoulder; magic is all Earth Elemental spells of levels 1-2.', 'None named in his entry.', 'A demon clerk of immense age who climbed to second in command of the 7th Kingdom and now governs Hubei as its Regent under a special Mandate. He usually appears as a richly dressed blackened Yama King skeleton whose bones are plainly those of a Horned Demon Overlord, and at ease he wears a Demon Lord''s horns, spines and scales.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.38-39'),
('chi-chou-lu', 'Chi Chou Lu', NULL, 'Taoist Immortal of the Shang Zheng Ye Sect', 'rifts', 'Taoist Immortal (human implied; the book does not state a race)', '9th level Taoist Immortal, 6th level Mystic Martial Artist, 4th level Enlightened Scholar', 9, 'Unprincipled', NULL, '5 ft 5 in (1.6 m)', '145 lbs (65.2 kg)', '{"IQ":24,"ME":19,"MA":15,"PS":21,"PP":23,"PE":19,"PB":16,"Spd":17}', 144, 65, NULL, 240, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The book gives him a short stat line only: no Horror Factor, M.D.C., I.S.P., attacks, bonuses, abilities, magic or skills are printed. The text also calls him Chou Lu.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Has bound his fortunes to the Demon Regent and serves as one of his most trusted counsellors; it was he who pressed for Wudangshan to be closed to demons.', 'Tai Shan Chun, the Demon Regent, whom he advises; the disciples and students he brought into the Regent''s service.', NULL, 'An Immortal of the Shang Zheng Ye Sect who went over to the Demon Regent of Hubei and took his followers with him. He lives inside the Walls of Wuchang.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.39-40'),
('ast-oth', 'Ast-Oth', NULL, 'Gargoyle Mage of the Z''grath Clan', 'rifts', 'Gargoyle', NULL, NULL, 'Anarchist', NULL, '18 ft (5.5 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":17,"ME":21,"MA":14,"PS":31,"PP":27,"PE":26,"PB":6,"Spd":17}', NULL, NULL, 400, 300, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Spd 17 is running; flying Spd is 90. The book gives him a short stat line only: no level, Horror Factor, attacks, bonuses or magic are printed, and it points to Rifts World Book 5: Triax & the NGR for Gargoyles in general.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Ambitious; he is manoeuvring to be recognised as the official voice of the Gargoyles of Rifts China.', 'Tai Shan Chun, the Demon Regent; the Gargoyles who have settled in Hubei, in the ruins of Xiangfan, across forty years.', NULL, 'A Gargoyle spell caster of the Z''grath Clan and an ally of the Demon Regent. He hopes to speak for all of China''s Gargoyles, many of whom now live in Hubei.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.40'),
('zhua-zhao', 'Zhua Zhao', NULL, 'lord of the Black Fang Giant clan (Clan Lord of the Hei Ch''ih Chu)', 'rifts', 'Hei Ch''ih Chu (Black Fang Giant)', NULL, NULL, 'Diabolic', NULL, '34 ft (10.3 m)', '2,800 lbs (1260 kg)', '{"IQ":12,"ME":11,"MA":12,"PS":42,"PP":15,"PE":27,"PB":3,"Spd":9}', NULL, NULL, 265, 180, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The book gives him a short stat line only: no level, Horror Factor, attacks, bonuses or abilities are printed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Asserts that leadership of China''s Black Fang Giants is his by birth.', 'Tai Shan Chun, the Demon Regent; no fewer than 600 Black Fang Giants idling in Hankou, where they have acquired a taste for the local black heroin.', NULL, 'Hereditary claimant to rule the Black Fang Giants of China, enormous pale armoured humanoids with black teeth. He and his clan are allies of the Demon Regent of Hubei.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.40'),
('ping-teng', 'Ping Teng', NULL, '8th Yama King', 'rifts', 'Yama King (the book prints no Race line)', 'Effective level: 6th level Necromancer', 6, 'Aberrant evil', '13,000 years; a Yama King for only about two thousand of them', 'Variable, usually about 12 ft (3.6 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":9,"ME":8,"MA":4,"PS":55,"PP":17,"PE":27,"PB":10,"Spd":11}', NULL, NULL, 8500, 3700, 180, NULL, 18, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":4,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"pull":2,"roll":1}', 'P.S. is Supernatural, fed by his paranoia and violent moods. I.Q. 9 is his insanity: sane, it would be far higher. Horror Factor 18 is above the other Yama Kings'' because he is a lunatic. Five physical attacks; a spell counts as two. All bonuses are already lowered for his madness. +2 vs psionic attacks, +10 save vs magic, 20% to charm/impress. Immune to Horror Factor, possession and mind control. His old abilities are lost to madness: Necromancy and his natural powers are all he can focus on. Nobody can say whether he would fight in person; his court keeps him out of battle and fights in his place.', '[{"name":"Literacy: Chinese (all)","pct":98},{"name":"Art","pct":60},{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":15},{"name":"Dance","pct":80},{"name":"Prowl","pct":57},{"name":"Sing","pct":15},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":28},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":30},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":48},{"name":"Temple Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":28},{"name":"Temple Lore: Meditation","pct":9},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":29},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":58}]', 'Speaks and understands every language by magic. Every skill but his reading of Chinese is cut down by insanity.', 'Nightvision 1000 ft (305 m), sees the invisible. Dimensional teleport 75%, down from 98% before his madness. Immune to S.D.C. weapons, fire, cold, poison and disease. Man-made M.D. weapons, psionics and magic do half damage, and their penalties and effects run half as long. Bio-regeneration: 1D6x10 M.D.C. each melee round, doubled on a ley line or wherever magic gives off negative energy, and only 1D6 a round where positive energy or chi fills the place. Never needs sleep, rest, drink or food; lately he craves strong incense, peaches and peach blossom where he once liked human blood. Demons: any demon whose name he knows must come at once and obey; one unknown to him may resist the call on a save vs magical summoning of 15 or better, and may refuse an order by rolling above his Horror Factor (18), though in his presence most obey anyway. Metamorphosis: takes any shape in an instant, a dragon included, with that shape''s natural abilities added to his own; at present he favours an old scholar, a wizened priest or a sorcerer. VULNERABILITIES: the Mandate of the Jade Emperor, on the same three terms as the other Yama Kings: 1. Point of Correction, 2. Accusation of Neglect, 3. Dissolution of Godhood. He breaks the Mandate openly, so his demons never leave him alone and silence anyone who tries a Point of Correction.', 'All Necromancy spells and nothing else; every other spell is forgotten. Demonic curses: all, but he must save vs insanity (15 or higher) to lay one; on a failure the curse lands on himself and takes him an hour or more to dispel. Martial Art Powers: none at present.', 'Empathic Transmission (6) and Mind Block Auto-Defense', NULL, NULL, 'Xian Jung Long Ku, the Immortal Dragon Bone: a broken rib of a dragon that glitters like a gem, worn on a chain at his neck and nearly always clutched in his left hand. Waking without it sends him into a panic. The book prints no numbers for it and leaves its tie to his madness unknown.', NULL, 'Unpredictable, suspicious of everyone and fixated on the rooms around him; he shuts a door 8, 28 or 31 times over as a ritual.', 'No real friend or loyal servant: his attendants stay out of fear and greed, and many would kill anybody who tried to cure him. Zu Daozheng, his Chamberlain, is the strongest Demon Lord in the Province and decides who reaches the king; the book prints no numbers for him.', NULL, 'The eighth Yama King, ruler of Chuanxi Province from a throne at Chongqing, whose madness has left him little but raw strength and Necromancy. He usually appears as a blackened skeleton in rumpled or missing clothes, his bones swelling and shrinking without his noticing. The Demon Lords under him keep him enthroned because it profits them.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.41-43'),
('tu-shis', 'Tu Shis', NULL, '9th Yama King', 'rifts', 'Yama King (the book prints no Race line)', '20th level Chi Mage, 10th level Necromancer, 10th level Mystic Martial Artist', 20, 'Aberrant evil', '5,600 years; a Yama King for 900 of them', 'Changes to suit the occasion: 20 ft (6.1 m) or more to impress, about 6 ft (1.8 m) or slightly over when receiving visitors', NULL, '{"IQ":18,"ME":30,"MA":21,"PS":31,"PP":29,"PE":30,"PB":22,"Spd":21}', NULL, NULL, 9800, 5500, 300, NULL, 15, '{"attacks":10,"initiative":8,"strike":12,"parry":11,"dodge":8,"pull":10,"roll":4}', 'P.S. is Supernatural. Ten attacks; each use of magic counts as two. +12 save vs psionics/insanity, +12 save vs magic, 80% to charm/impress. Immune to Horror Factor and possession. Like his peers he leaves fighting to underlings.', '[{"name":"Literacy: Chinese (all)","pct":98},{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":90},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":95},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Temple Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":98}]', 'Speaks and understands every language by magic. Every ancient W.P.; W.P. Energy Pistol, W.P. Energy Rifle and W.P. Heavy Energy, at 10th level.', 'Nightvision 1000 ft (305 m), sees the invisible. Dimensional teleport 90%. Immune to S.D.C. weapons, fire, cold, poison and disease. Man-made M.D. weapons, psionics and magic do half damage. Bio-regeneration: 8D6 M.D.C. each melee round, doubled on a ley line or wherever magic gives off negative energy, and only 1D6 a round in a place of positive energy or chi. Never needs sleep, rest, drink or food, though he will eat and drink out of courtesy. Dragon Lines: he slows or quickens the flow of nearby ley lines, from dormant up to the strength of a Vernal or Autumnal Equinox, and lengthens or shortens a line by as much as 9 miles (14.4 km) to bend it toward himself or away (the book points to Rifts RPG pp. 162-163). Demons: any demon whose name he knows must come at once and obey; one unknown to him may resist the call on a save vs magical summoning of 15 or better, and may refuse an order by rolling above his Horror Factor (15), though in his presence most obey anyway. Metamorphosis: takes any shape in an instant, a dragon included, with that shape''s natural abilities added to his own. VULNERABILITIES: the Mandate of the Jade Emperor, much of which he has thrown out, so he counts himself exposed. The three conditions apply to him as they do to his peers: 1. Point of Correction; 2. Accusation of Neglect; 3. Dissolution of Godhood. Against the second and third, however, he has ready a Petition of Grievances to the Heavenly Court, written in Cloud Characters, which halts most proceedings: he formally names the accuser an Agent of the Jade Emperor and insists the Petition accounts for his lapses, which buys time to argue the accuser round or to remind them the Petition has to be carried to the Jade Emperor.', 'Every spell Invocation, the Spells of Legend among them, and all Necromancy. Demonic curses: all. Martial Art Powers: Ba Gua Kungfu at 10th level, Hsien Hsia Kungfu at 10th level, Tien-Hsueh Kungfu at 8th level.', 'Master Psychic, I.S.P. 300: Mind Block Auto-Defense and every Super Psionic power. The book prints no cost for any power.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Attentive, well spoken and perceptive. He tires of people quickly and hides it: a private signal brings an attendant to interrupt.', 'Chu O, the Crimson Moth of myth (printed 46-47), which he keeps on show unconscious as proof of his power; the book does not say how he keeps it so. Displayed as a bright moth the span of an open hand, at true size it is bigger than an elephant. 18,000 M.D.C.; +10 save vs magic; no conventional S.D.C. or M.D. weapon hurts it, only psionics, magic and magic weapons; it can be ridden as an invulnerable mount. At 0 M.D.C. it lies senseless 2D6 hours; at 1000 below zero it turns into a rainbow that lasts 1D4 hours and fades, and it is reborn 24 hours after any destruction. A Lore: Chinese Mythology roll recalls it as the creature that once beat the Jade Emperor. Hu Fen Pao, the White Lead Leopards (printed 47): the nine survivors (5 male, 4 female) of an order of assassins out of a Hell older than the Yama Kings, who serve by contract, may turn a job down, are normally hired one at a time, and live in the City of Accidental Death, the single Hell Tu Shis left untouched. Each is a leopard-headed human figure or a giant leopard of dull white metal spotted with dark corrosion, pale and blotched when in human shape. Alignment Aberrant. I.Q. 1D6+12, M.A. 2D6+12, M.E. 2D6+12, P.S. 2D6+20 (Supernatural), P.P. 2D6+16, P.E. 2D6+12, P.B. 2D6+12, Spd 2D6+24. M.D.C. 1D6x10+180. Horror Factor 14. Weight 2,000 lbs (900 kg) as metal, 400 lbs (180 kg) as flesh. Master Psionic, I.S.P. 3D6x10+23, with every Physical, Sensitive and Super power; 7th level Chinese Chi Mage. Nine physical attacks a melee; as a leopard the bite does 5D6 and each claw 4D6, S.D.C. or M.D. according to the opponent. Besides attribute bonuses: +3 initiative, +4 strike, +2 parry and dodge, +5 pull punch, +2 save vs psionics/insanity, +4 save vs magic, +8 save vs Horror Factor, +7 save vs possession, mind control and illusions. They know a contracted target on sight, run without tiring at 45 mph (79 km as printed), leap 30 ft (9.1 m) up or across (twice that with a run-up), track by sight 80% and by smell 50% (+20% on a blood trail), Prowl 60%, have nightvision 300 ft (91.5 m), see the invisible, and speak every language while reading none. Never-Dying Servants (printed 47): he copies Yen Lo''s Soul Deal to recruit, with notices throughout Guangxi promising revival after each death to whoever joins his army at the palace in Nanning; everything else is as written for Yen Lo (printed 30), and no numbers are given here.', NULL, 'The ninth Yama King, ruler of Guangxi Province from Nanning and the most ambitious of them: he means to rule China and then the Earth, and is patient about it. Officially a blackened skeleton in embroidered silk, he more and more shows himself as a black-skinned man with Asian features, and when threatened becomes a horned demon with spiked armor, a third eye in the forehead and a second pair of arms. He has largely dropped the tormenting of the dead to retrain demons as soldiers and put the dead to work.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.45-47'),
('meng-po-niang-niang', 'Meng P''o Niang Niang', NULL, 'Lady Meng of the Terrace of Oblivion', 'rifts', 'Immortal goddess (the book prints no Race line)', '30th level Chinese Alchemist', 30, 'Principled', '2,850 years', 'Slightly over 4 ft (1.2 m)', 'Less than 75 lbs (33.7 kg)', '{"IQ":23,"ME":19,"MA":22,"PS":23,"PP":24,"PE":22,"PB":14,"Spd":15}', NULL, NULL, 1750, 8800, 400, NULL, 10, '{"attacks":10,"initiative":7,"strike":10,"parry":12,"dodge":14,"pull":7,"roll":9}', 'P.S. is Supernatural. The book prints her 10 as a Horror/Awe Factor. Ten attacks; each use of magic counts as two. +10 save vs psionics/insanity, +12 save vs magic, 64% to charm/impress. Thought to be the most powerful Chinese Alchemist alive. She has no interest in combat beyond trying her Tai Chi on rude attackers.', '[{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":90},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":90},{"name":"History: China","pct":90},{"name":"Research","pct":90},{"name":"Dowsing","pct":90},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":90},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":90},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":90}]', 'Speaks and understands every language by magic. Reads Chinese and has every Medical, Science and Lore skill, at 98%.', 'Nightvision 400 ft (122 m), sees the invisible. Dimensional teleport 70%. Immune to S.D.C. weapons, fire, cold, poison and disease; Mega-Damage cold and fire do half damage. Bio-regeneration: 6D6 M.D.C. each melee round, doubled on a ley line or wherever magic gives off positive energy. Never needs sleep, rest, drink or food, but likes mortal comforts. Command Demons: every demon, Demon Lords and Overlords included, is subject to her direct order; she cannot summon them, and most run or keep clear once they know she is close. Those who do face her nearly always obey, and the rare one that resists needs 17 or better to save, even if Horror Factor cannot otherwise touch it. VULNERABILITIES: full damage from M.D. weapons, psionics and magic. Her power rests on a Mandate of the Jade Emperor, but her duty depends on the Yama Kings bringing her the dead, so she has made no error and no penalty for failure can reach her.', 'Every spell invocation, among them Barrier of Thoth, Crimson Wall of Lictalon, Doppleganger, Ley Line Resurrection, Metropolis and Sanctuary. Demonic curses: none. Martial Art Powers: Xian Tai Chi Chuan at 18th level.', 'Master Psychic, I.S.P. 400: every Healing, Physical and Sensitive power, and Hydrokinesis, Mind Block Auto-Defense and Psychosomatic Disease. The book prints no cost for any power.', NULL, NULL, 'The Five-Flavored Tea of Forgetfulness, also called the Brew of Oblivion (printed 48), which she brews out of local waters and herbs. A mortal drinker is rid of trauma, painful memory, insanity, disease, infirmity and deformity, and with them of identity and every tie to the past: friends, family, goals and trade are gone. An adult keeps 1D4+2 skills, the most important ones, fixed at the level they had, and begins again as a teenage adult in a new O.C.C. at level one, free to take any alignment. Nothing reverses it. The tea does not keep long. She also makes healing and life-enhancing elixirs and poisons for rats and mice. The book tells G.M.s to use the tea with care.', NULL, 'Kindly, always smiling and endlessly compassionate, with no fear at all; being attacked only makes her merrier.', NULL, NULL, 'A tiny, grandmotherly immortal who keeps the Terrace of Oblivion near the ruins of Chengdu and brews the tea that wipes souls clean for rebirth. She is a cheerful old woman in modest embroidered silk with dyed black hair and smile lines, kept nimble by thousands of years of Xian Tai Chi. No demon can refuse her order, yet she wants only to be left in peace.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.48-49'),
('huang-di', 'Huang Di', NULL, 'Emperor of the 11th Kingdom of Hell', 'rifts', 'human', 'Unknown, at least 9th level', 9, 'Aberrant evil', 'Unknown', '5 ft 5 in (1.65 m)', 'Under 150 lbs (67.5 kg)', '{"IQ":20,"ME":17,"MA":19,"PS":25,"PP":19,"PE":17,"PB":10,"Spd":13}', 86, 105, NULL, 22, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"parry":3,"dodge":2,"roll":2}', 'Horror Factor is printed as None: he looks like an average man. He can survive two M.D. points of damage, and adds conventional or magic armor on top. +4 save vs psionics/insanity (the book prints "vs" twice). Save vs magic: the bonus line prints "+6 to save vs magic" and later "+2 to save vs magic and poison"; the book prints both and both are recorded here as printed. +5 save vs Horror Factor, 90% to charm/impress. He stays out of combat whatever it costs, stepping behind his bodyguards.', '[{"name":"Language and Literacy: Chinese and most dialects","pct":98},{"name":"Calligraphy","pct":95},{"name":"Tea Appreciation","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Classical Studies","pct":90},{"name":"Lore: Chinese Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Temple Lore: Feng Shui/Geomancy","pct":98},{"name":"Temple Lore: Meditation","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":90},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":90},{"name":"Climbing","pct":90},{"name":"Swimming","pct":90}]', 'Climbing printed 90/80%. Every Military skill at 90%, leaving out space, ship and trap combat. Most Ancient Chinese W.P.s.', 'Nothing beyond his attributes and the fact that he does not seem to age. He is as easily hurt as any ordinary human and heals at the ordinary rate. VULNERABILITIES: he is mortal, with rivals among both demons and gods, and his obsession and cruelty at times undo his own plans. No Mandate or other document binds him as one binds the Yama Kings.', 'None; he orders others to work magic for him. Demonic curses: none. Martial Art Powers: none printed.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'No personal weapon is printed. He wears protective armor, conventional or magic, and treats magic and technology as two separate resources for his army and defenses; he covets high-tech weapons and machines, magic items and ancient artifacts.', NULL, 'A dictator: arrogant and gushing by turns. He charms on first meeting and the charm does not last.', 'Creatures and Followers. The Terra-Cotta Warriors, his army, which have creature rows of their own (terra-cotta-warrior and tiny-terra-cotta-warrior). The book gives three differing counts of them: about 800,000 on the province''s Population line (printed 49); hundreds of thousands, perhaps more, in his own entry; and at least 100,000 and perhaps two or three times that in the creature section (printed 51). His entry puts them down to ancient rune magic or Bio-Wizardry in theory and says they are being altered and improved. The Chi Magic Technicians: a dozen or more dead or damned inventors he rescued, who made the Terra-Cotta Warriors and his other innovations. No numbers are printed for them beyond that count.', 'Gong Gong, a demon more than 60 ft (18.3 m) tall and his sworn enemy, who has assaulted the Great Wall of Shanxi for twenty years and pulls back after taking thousands of points of Mega-Damage; he and his snake-like servant Xiang Yao have disappeared into Rifts China. The Immortal Taoists: Huang Di burned most of the Taoist Library more than 2,000 years ago, and every Taoist Sect wants him destroyed.', 'The First Emperor of China reborn, a mortal man who runs Shanxi Province from Xi''an as a slave state and works his people to death. He is an ordinary-looking Asian man in loose black silk trousers and a jacket with a gold dragon across the back. He avoids every fight and leans on bodyguards, hired magic and his Terra-Cotta army.', 'Rifts World Book 24: China 1 p.49-51');
